d, then we cannot remove the parent because it would cause removal of a non-removable node. So we skip.\n\n- Also check required symbols as before.\n\nImplementation steps:\n- Build tree.\n- Precompute for each node a list of its descendants (or compute on fly).\n- Maintain removed set.\n- Process nodes in sorted order: depth descending, ID ascending.\n- For each node:\n  - If node already removed: skip.\n  - If not removable: skip (as candidate, not removable).\n  - Compute all nodes that would be removed if we remove this node: node itself plus all its descendants that are not already removed. Call this set `to_remove`.\n  - Check: for each node in to_remove, is it removable? (node's removable flag). If any is not removable, skip (cannot remove).\n  - Check required symbols: Compute new symbol set after removing these nodes. That is, current set of symbols (from all nodes not in removed) minus symbols of nodes in to_remove. If this new set still contains all required symbols, then removal is valid.\n  - If valid: add node id to removed_node_ids list (order). Add all nodes in to_remove to removed set. (Note: we only record the direct removal decision, not the descendant IDs. But the descendant nodes will be considered later as they are already removed, so they won't be processed again.)\n- After loop: retained nodes = all nodes not in removed set. Sort by ID. Return {\"removed_node_ids\": list_of_removed_ids, \"retained_node_ids\": sorted_retained_ids}.\n\nBut we must also consider that when we remove a node, we might remove descendants that were previously considered but not removed because they would violate requirements on their own. Now with the ancestor removal, the requirement check passes because the required symbol might be present elsewhere. That's fine.\n\nCheck test from fixtures: We need to verify with given examples? Not provided expected outputs, but we can infer.\n\nWe'll implement solve(case) accordingly. Use only standard library. No mutation of case input.\n\nWe need to output Python source code as a string inside JSON under \"implementation\". Ensure JSON escaping.\n\nWrite code carefully. Use proper variable names. Indentation inside string.\n\nWe'll produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2172,"completion_tokens":4632,"total_tokens":6804,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3898},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":124},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}